    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 537 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3809\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 537 of the laws of 2008,\namending the education law relating to a restricted dental faculty\nlicense, in relation to making such provisions permanent\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo make permanent current provisions of law concerning licensure of\nforeign-trained dentists who are employed as full-time faculty members\nat a New York State dental school.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 2 eliminates the expiration date (currently February 1, 2021)\nfor a restricted dental faculty license.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDentists educated outside the United States are eligible for a\nrestricted dental faculty license in New York State, but current law has\nthem set to expire in 2021. The Restricted Dental Faculty Licensure\nprogram has been very successful. Dental schools face great difficulty\nin luring domestically educated dentists into academic dentistry, as\ncompensation for these positions is much lower than dental practice. The\nhigh debt loads incurred by American dental school graduates coupled\nwith the salary differential only compounds the difficulty faced by\ndental schools in filling these positions.  Opening up dental faculty\npositions to more candidates while preserving SED oversight and regu-\nlations will provide stability to the dental community in New York.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
